# Android (client/android, created locally by `npx cap add android` -- not
# generated by anything that runs in this environment). The android/ project
# itself is meant to be committed once it exists (standard Capacitor
# convention -- it's not regenerated by `cap sync`), just not its local
# build/machine-specific artifacts.
client/android/app/build/
client/android/build/
client/android/.gradle/
client/android/local.properties
client/android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/

# Generated run artifacts from server/src/scripts/evalChatEngine.js -- real
# output worth keeping locally as evidence for the paper, but regenerated
# per-run rather than committed.
server/eval-results/
